---
description: When landlord onboarding completes — and whenever residents/vendors are added later — automatically start outbound activation. Tenant welcome SMS uses a 3-attempt delivery retry schedule.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Onboarding completion → automatic activation

When a landlord finishes setup (`completeOnboarding`), **everyone listed in that onboarding run** is automatically started on their outbound activation flow. Landlords should not have to click per person.

The same tenant welcome SMS also runs when a resident is **added after setup** (Residents / User Management → Add resident), if they have a phone.

## Rule

| Listed during onboarding | Automatic action on complete |
|---|---|
| Resident / tenant with a phone | Tenant welcome / activation SMS (`sendTenantActivationSms`) |
| Vendor with phone and/or email | Unique vendor verification invite (`sendVendorInvite`) via SMS, email, or both |

| Added after onboarding | Automatic action |
|---|---|
| Resident with a phone | Same welcome / YES SMS (`activateTenantAfterAdd`) |
| Resident created without phone, phone added later | Same welcome SMS when phone first saved (`phoneNewlyAdded`) |
| Vendor with phone and/or email | Same verification invite (`inviteVendorAfterAdd` → `sendVendorInvite`) from Vendors list / User Management Add Vendor |
| Vendor (Find External Vendor) | `sendVendorInvite` via Invite to verify |

## Tenant activation SMS retries

| Attempt | When |
|---|---|
| 1 | Immediate on onboarding complete / add / phone first set |
| 2 | 24 hours after attempt 1, only if attempt 1 was a **delivery** failure |
| 3 | 72 hours after attempt 1 (final automatic retry) |
| After 3 failures | Stop; `activation_status = action_required`; notify landlord |

**Retry only** on delivery problems (invalid number, carrier/network/provider errors).

**Never auto-retry** when the resident replied STOP, already opted in / activated, or the phone number changed (landlord must update + **Resend Welcome Text**).

YES/START → `activated` (stop retries). STOP → `opted_out` (stop retries).

Landlord-facing statuses: Activated · Waiting for Resident · Delivery Failed (Retry X of 3) · Action Required.

Manual **Resend Welcome Text** (Action Required) restarts the retry sequence after a successful send.

Cron: `check-tenant-activation-retries`. Attempts audited in `tenant_activation_attempts`.

## Requirements

- Pass each vendor’s `vendorId` so form submit updates that roster profile.
- Mint a **unique** verification link per vendor invite.
- Best-effort delivery: never block finishing setup (or saving a new resident) on SMS/email failure; surface a combined `activationWarning` / add-resident warning and log graph events for the activity feed.
- Skip people with no usable contact info.
- Follow the Ulo communication writing standard for all outbound copy.
- Idempotent: skip if welcome already sent and waiting (`activation_sms_sent_at` / `waiting`) unless landlord `resend`.

## Where it lives

- Orchestration: `src/lib/landlordOnboarding.ts` → `completeOnboarding`
- Post-onboarding add: `src/api/tenantActivation.ts` → `activateTenantAfterAdd` (wired from `AdminResidentsDashboard` / `AdminUserManagementDashboard`)
- Post-onboarding vendor add: `src/api/vendorVerification.ts` → `inviteVendorAfterAdd` (wired from `VendorFormModal`)
- Tenant send + retries: `supabase/functions/_shared/sms/tenantActivation.ts` / `send-tenant-activation` / `check-tenant-activation-retries`
- Status UI: `src/lib/tenantActivationStatus.ts`, Residents / User Management / resident detail
- Vendor send: `src/api/vendorVerification.ts` → `send-vendor-invite`

Manual “Invite vendor” controls on the vendors list and vendor profile are removed —
verification starts automatically at onboarding complete **and** when a vendor is added
later with phone/email. Find External Vendor can still call `sendVendorInvite` explicitly.
